1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:04,080
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,181
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:07,720
Always stand up!

4
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:09,897
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:11,400
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:15,677
We'll get past every wall that's
in our wake, go without hesitation!

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:16,800
Hands up!

8
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,217
To get to the answers we're looking for.

10
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:34,897
We came to this new world
believing that surely someday.

11
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:37,977
We just might find the way.

12
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,357
Our bonds won't waver.

14
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,880
Let's head on towards.

16
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,697
A bright new future.

17
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:56,537
Now everybody lift your hands up.

18
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,597
Sing about what you are dreaming.

19
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,217
Always stand up.

20
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,417
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

21
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

22
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

23
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,420
Let's head on never stopping.

24
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,337
Only look up.

25
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,337
Keep your head up, way up high.

26
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,037
Always step up.

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,017
If waves are rough, jump to the sky.

28
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:18,797
Never give up.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,777
Our wishes, they will come together.

30
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:23,180
And lead us on for the future.

31
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:27,837
We drift on riding the waves.

32
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,717
Towards another shore day by day.

33
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,497
There are many meetings, many goodbyes.

34
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,840
Underneath the flag we fly.

35
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,697
I'll remember the pain within.

36
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,857
I'll keep it in my heart forever.

37
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:47,977
And never take it lightly.

38
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,837
But I won't surrender.

39
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,037
This freedom I will keep in mind.

40
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,637
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

41
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:57,437
Now everybody lift your hands up.

42
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,517
Sing about what you are dreaming.

43
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,177
Always stand up.

44
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,337
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

45
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,877
Gotta keep up.

46
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,237
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

47
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,680
Let's head on, never stop it.

48
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:14,317
Only look up, keep your
head up way up high.

49
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,937
Always step up, if brains
are rubbed up to the sky.

50
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:21,637
Never give up, our wishes,
they will come together.

51
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:24,140
And lead us on for the future.

52
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,120
Hands up.

53
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,574
Nami's been kidnapped?

54
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:36,329
It was my fault, they were huge,
but I never saw them coming

55
00:02:36,860 --> 00:02:40,860
They showed up out of nowhere,
attacked, then they left.

56
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:43,784
First it was centaurs,
now we've got giants too?

57
00:02:43,940 --> 00:02:46,175
What kind of messed up island is this?

58
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:47,180
An ambush.

59
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:48,971
So they were tracking us.

60
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,497
That means they're professionals.

61
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:52,060
They must be. Huh?

62
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:53,200
I'm confused.

63
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:56,200
So they didn't come to save Gatorbeard?

64
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,360
Definitely not.

65
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:00,974
Seems they wanted to kill us
and take the children back.

66
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:05,800
But then their master, he
made them kill Brownbeard.

67
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:07,688
They were on the same side.

68
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:09,900
Brownbeard was so loyal, too.

69
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:13,160
The Master wouldn't harm children.

70
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:15,140
He's a one-hearted savior.

71
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:19,557
We don't know much about this Master guy,
but there are two things I'm sure of.

72
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,700
That he's evil and he's dangerous.

73
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:23,480
He can't take them.

74
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:24,997
Who knows what he'll do?

75
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,937
And that's not the only problem.

76
00:03:27,020 --> 00:03:28,977
Nami's still trapped in Frankie's body.

77
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:31,119
I'm really worried about her, guys.

78
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:34,180
Yeah, I'll save her somehow.

79
00:03:34,860 --> 00:03:35,690
Wow.

80
00:03:35,773 --> 00:03:37,140
All right, you look after the kids.

81
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:38,790
Luffy, wait.

82
00:03:38,873 --> 00:03:39,703
Don't forget.

83
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,340
It's my body they took.

84
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:44,567
Hey, Chopper, I can't
fight in this rat suit.

85
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:47,537
Give me one of those magic beans
that turns you into a badass.

86
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:48,977
And make it quick, would you?

87
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:49,890
What bean?

88
00:03:49,973 --> 00:03:51,017
Wait, the rumble ball?

89
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:52,077
But that's a drug.

90
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:53,680
You can't control it.

91
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:55,135
Not on the first try.

92
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,341
Of course I can.

93
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:59,717
I'm a super-powered cyborg
with the heart of a champion.

94
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,257
Now hand over the goods, damn it.

95
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:04,097
We don't have a lot of time to
sit here and argue about it.

96
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:05,010
Ugh.

97
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:07,557
Listen, that thing will
make you a monster.

98
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:08,820
But not for long.

99
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,257
After just three minutes,
you'll be worn out.

100
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:14,900
Try to do Kong fu point
like I did earlier and...

101
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:21,680
Way too early!

102
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:27,220
Come on, Franky, follow me!

103
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,640
Whoa! Stop it!

104
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:42,642
Why are you trying to squish me?

105
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:45,920
Whoa! Whoa!

106
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:50,660
Ricky! I told you! Be careful!

107
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:55,200
Maybe we should've had him stay here?

108
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:59,120
He's dangerous right now, but
once the rumble ball wears off,

109
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,737
he'll be too weak to move.

110
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:02,114
Then he'll be useless.

111
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:10,280
I don't know where he got it,

112
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:14,320
but this cyborg Franky fellow
appears to have Vegapunk's laser

113
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:17,037
weapon attached to his body.

114
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:21,077
After I cut that garish robot to
pieces and extract the laser system,

115
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:24,477
his body will be nothing but a
worthless pile of scrap metal.

116
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:26,920
Prepare the incinerator. Yes, sir.

117
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:29,057
Those would be ship thieves.

118
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:30,597
You know, the ones from the Navy.

119
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:31,510
What of them?

120
00:05:31,593 --> 00:05:33,020
Oh, right.

121
00:05:33,340 --> 00:05:35,634
The battle's raging out of control now.

122
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:37,270
Oh?

123
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:40,380
Then we're having trouble.

124
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:42,460
I mean...

125
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:47,460
In that case...

126
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:54,600
Master?

127
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,137
Ah, yes.

128
00:05:59,220 --> 00:06:00,677
This will do nicely.

129
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:03,840
I'm sure the Navy will make
excellent test subjects.

130
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:08,680
It's a golden opportunity.

131
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:14,457
Contact all the centaurs
currently on patrol.

132
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:16,497
Better make it quick. Right.

133
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:19,457
Tell our soldiers to evacuate at once.

134
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:21,960
Unless they want to die, that is!

135
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,720
What do you want from me?

136
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:36,190
Perverts!

137
00:06:36,273 --> 00:06:37,103
Let me go!

138
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:39,677
Keep your filthy paws to
yourself, you hear me?

139
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:42,820
Listen, I understand that
I'm cute and voluptuous,

140
00:06:43,140 --> 00:06:45,177
and you wanted me all to yourselves.

141
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:46,800
This guy is different.

142
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:50,257
Hey, whatever he's
into, it's cool with me.

143
00:06:50,340 --> 00:06:52,620
You'll pay for this, jerks!

144
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:54,662
Just wait until Luffy gets here!

145
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:57,400
He'll kick your hairy
butts into next week!

146
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:01,600
Hey, keep your voice down.

147
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:03,537
Noisy prisoners are...

148
00:07:03,620 --> 00:07:04,740
Not cool.

149
00:07:05,620 --> 00:07:09,340
On the other hand, the laser
weapon built into your body is...

150
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:10,890
Very cool.

151
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:15,480
And the reward for bringing
it to our master will be...

152
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:18,500
Extra cool.

153
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:22,300
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

154
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:28,320
This wind is so cool.

155
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:30,940
Almost too cool.

156
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:36,360
Get some clothes!

157
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:39,460
To someone your size,

158
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:43,037
a shot from one of our rifles is
like being hit by a cannonball.

159
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:45,340
And these are filled with poison gas.

160
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:47,857
Our targets never see it coming either.

161
00:07:47,940 --> 00:07:53,537
as for your friend of course he'll
come we set a trap to lure him

162
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:58,040
here he won't be able to resist
following giant footprints in the snow

163
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:08,817
sweet giant footprints
in the snow how easily

164
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:11,312
i should follow them this is way too easy

165
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:16,240
Hey, quit it, Franky!

166
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,940
How many times do I gotta tell you? Huh?

167
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:26,324
Oh, there's no more footprints!

168
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:35,780
Luffy and Chopper?

169
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:38,160
No, wait, that's Franky! Nami!

170
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,400
Be careful!

171
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:42,938
Their foe's hiding!

172
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:49,760
Ready, Scotch? Ready.

173
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:52,767
Pretty Uncle of him not
to notice the cliff.

174
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:56,020
Are those spikes?

175
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:59,060
It's all over.

176
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,900
Not a cool way to die.

177
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,597
Armament! Hard name!

178
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:08,840
Gum-Gum Candy!

179
00:09:21,660 --> 00:09:25,120
Ah, he's a bit trickier than the rest.

180
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:26,680
Gum-Gum!

181
00:09:27,660 --> 00:09:28,880
Stop right there!

182
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:30,660
Hooray!

183
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:39,505
Rayleigh told me it's a waste to
just use this move for defense.

184
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:41,680
Let's see, what did he say?

185
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:46,720
Shake the bullets and send them all
right back to him twice as hard!

186
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:50,700
Now, Kuma Kuma, fire the ground!

187
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:57,030
Rock!

188
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:05,700
What did I do to you?

189
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:07,680
Lay off, Franky!

190
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:09,764
We've got bigger problems here!

191
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:13,100
Now I'm burning up.

192
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:16,620
They might lose their cool,
but I won't lose mine.

193
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:20,070
Franky!

194
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:24,500
The cool thing about mountains is
they can be turned into weapons.

195
00:10:34,060 --> 00:10:35,040
Watch out!

196
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:37,376
The top of that nut's falling on you!

197
00:10:37,660 --> 00:10:39,680
You won't be breaking heads up!

198
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:43,880
You'll never get away in time!

199
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:45,500
Look behind you!

200
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:46,640
He's gonna shoot!

201
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:50,517
All it takes is one of
these KYP canisters.

202
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:52,817
And you'll fall into a drunken stupor!

203
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:54,135
just like the others.

204
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:04,500
Frank, you did something useful!

205
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:11,950
Yeah!

206
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:14,140
Now you're getting it! Good job!

207
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:18,620
Oh, great!

208
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:20,192
We're back to this, huh?

209
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:21,580
Oh, God!

210
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,360
Elephant God!

211
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:31,929
You went straight to
that trick of the day!

212
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,270
Help!

213
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:36,550
Help!

214
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:39,640
Uh-oh.

215
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:41,700
Sorry, Chopper's buddy.

216
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:43,817
I'll get Chopper to fix you up later.

217
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:44,730
Wait.

218
00:11:44,813 --> 00:11:45,720
Never mind!

219
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:51,620
I told you before we have the
home-filled advantage in these mountains.

220
00:11:51,860 --> 00:11:53,840
Just give up. Luffy!

221
00:11:57,620 --> 00:11:58,450
Nami!

222
00:11:58,940 --> 00:11:59,770
Forget it.

223
00:11:59,900 --> 00:12:02,135
I can reach a lot higher than you can.

224
00:12:05,820 --> 00:12:08,800
Whoa, he's not kidding, but...

225
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:26,262
If I lose him in these mountains,
I'll never track him down again.

226
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:35,380
It's Law!

227
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:39,780
Ah, Trafalgar Law, the famous freeloader.

228
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:41,920
Cool, I'm glad you're here.

229
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:44,631
Straw Hat Luffy should be right behind me.

230
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:46,130
Rune.

231
00:12:57,660 --> 00:12:58,490
Ahhhhhhh!

232
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:14,060
Damn you!

233
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,080
That wasn't cool at all!

234
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,471
All right, counter-shock.

235
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:46,290
Agh!

236
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:48,540
Thank you! Ah!

237
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:50,880
Wait, change me back, creep!

238
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:52,690
Nami!

239
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,070
Hey!

240
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:57,760
It's you!

241
00:13:58,040 --> 00:13:59,805
Thanks for saving Nami, buddy!

242
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:02,420
Look, here's the thing, Straw Hat.

243
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:07,664
I came here because there's
something I want to discuss with you.

244
00:14:10,380 --> 00:14:13,380
I assume you landed on
Punk Hazard by accident.

245
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:17,620
But there's an important
key hiding on this island.

246
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:21,801
One that's powerful enough to throw
the new world into total chaos.

247
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:25,870
us.

248
00:14:25,953 --> 00:14:29,457
You see, there are only two
ways to live in the new world.

249
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:31,128
Fighting under the umbrella

250
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:36,597
of the four emperors or
fighting against them.

251
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:39,327
And you don't strike me
as the type who likes

252
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:43,857
to work under someone else.

253
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:47,237
Yep, that's right, I'm captain. I see.

254
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:48,260
Well then,

255
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:54,417
you can work with me huh like how us two

256
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:57,520
will take down one of the four emperors

257
00:15:02,980 --> 00:15:06,337
I've got a good plan so tell

258
00:15:06,420 --> 00:15:13,317
me so

259
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:16,317
let me

260
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:17,400
get this straight

261
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:20,337
We meet by chance on this crazy island,

262
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:24,017
and you ask us if we want to
fight an emperor out of the blue?

263
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:28,157
Look, I don't know what this sleazeball
is after, but I don't trust him.

264
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:29,769
He's up to no good, Luffy.

265
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:38,280
I'm not saying killing off
an emperor will be easy.

266
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:40,957
I just think our odds will be better if we

267
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:43,805
work together and plan
everything step by step.

268
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:45,480
What do you say?

269
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:47,372
This is your big chance.

270
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:50,937
Well, there's four of them, right?

271
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:52,138
So which one is it?

272
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:53,620
Which one is it?

273
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:55,537
Don't tell me you're thinking about it.

274
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:57,149
We can't team up with him.

275
00:16:06,180 --> 00:16:07,680
The name of our target.

276
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,720
Right, got it. Huh?

277
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:29,780
Sure, we're in.

278
00:16:36,940 --> 00:16:37,770
Wado?

279
00:16:37,853 --> 00:16:39,642
Team up with the heart, pirates!

280
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:41,720
What's the matter with you?

281
00:16:42,660 --> 00:16:43,542
Damn it, Luffy,

282
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:47,057
how did you manage to go completely insane
in the time you were out saving Nami?

283
00:16:47,140 --> 00:16:49,257
I mean, you weren't
even gone for that long.

284
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:50,170
Hold on.

285
00:16:50,253 --> 00:16:52,137
This psycho already
scared the crap out of me.

286
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:54,037
Now we have to trust him with our lives?

287
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:57,017
Now am I supposed to sleep
at night with him around?

288
00:16:57,100 --> 00:16:58,400
I told you, Luffy.

289
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:00,700
Let's just forget it. It's risky.

290
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:03,335
That's why nobody is on board with it.

291
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:05,557
It's better for us to do
things that are opaque.

292
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:06,470
She's right.

293
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:10,437
Besides, it's way too early to think
about challenging the four emperors.

294
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:12,320
We're just not ready yet!

295
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:13,700
Hey, Doc.

296
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,220
Fix this raccoon.

297
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:17,578
Raccoons aren't important right now!

298
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:21,580
That's me!

299
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:24,630
Silver!

300
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:29,820
What did you do to me?

301
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:37,760
Luffy, I will go along with
this, but we are all pirates.

302
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:42,026
And where you have pirates, well,
you're sure to have betrayal.

303
00:17:43,320 --> 00:17:45,580
Hey, are you going to betray me? No.

304
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:49,837
The rest of us are going
to need more than that!

305
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:50,750
Oh, come on.

306
00:17:50,980 --> 00:17:53,921
A pirate alliance sounds
like a lot of fun, right?

307
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:56,420
My gut says Traffy's an okay guy.

308
00:17:56,840 --> 00:17:59,311
But even if he's not, what's the big deal?

309
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:02,537
You guys were training
for the past two years.

310
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:04,032
I'll let you protect me.

311
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:08,940
Are you kidding me?

312
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:11,940
Aw, Luffy.

313
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:13,573
Look, now I'm flushing.

314
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:15,700
Thanks a lot, buddy.

315
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:16,977
I'm super flattered.

316
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:18,942
I promise we won't let you down.

317
00:18:20,060 --> 00:18:22,720
We're only awesome because it's our job.

318
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,353
There's no need to let her up, you know.

319
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:27,120
Yeah, don't worry, Luffy.

320
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:29,635
Whatever happens, we've got your back.

321
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:33,417
And hey, even if these other wimps
chicken out, you've always got me.

322
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:34,853
You're gonna be a fool.

323
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:38,630
Boom.

324
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:41,900
And shambles.

325
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:47,460
Dude! Huh?

326
00:18:48,820 --> 00:18:50,340
It's about time!

327
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:52,952
Man, it's good to be back in my own body!

328
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:55,780
Almost nobody else I'd rather be than me.

329
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:58,510
Super!

330
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:02,497
So you're back. That's great.

331
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:06,640
But don't ever take possession
of Chopper's body again. Ever.

332
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:08,720
I'm back.

333
00:19:09,780 --> 00:19:11,240
But I'm not happy.

334
00:19:12,180 --> 00:19:14,360
My body's all busted up now!

335
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:18,617
Wouldn't have killed you big jerks
to be a little more careful with it!

336
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:19,720
I'm sorry.

337
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:21,720
It was all Frankie's fault.

338
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:23,080
It was my fault?

339
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:25,957
You're the one who turned into
a monster and flipped out?

340
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:27,660
All I did was stop you!

341
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:31,957
With that same overpowered move you used
to beat that kraken, that was overkill!

342
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:33,740
Fine, you're both jerks!

343
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:35,640
Yeah, sorry, Chopper.

344
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:38,428
Well, at least you got
your own bodies back.

345
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:42,080
Why am I the only person
without my own body?

346
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:45,860
It's even funnier this way!

347
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:49,960
My good dummy!

348
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:54,500
Wow, I'm glad you're
enjoying it! Stop laughing!

349
00:19:55,060 --> 00:19:56,740
But it had to be you!

350
00:19:57,060 --> 00:19:59,137
Chopper and Franky were
both in the same place

351
00:19:59,220 --> 00:20:01,337
when our scary new friends
switched everyone back.

352
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:04,937
But since Sanji took your body with him
when he went looking for the samurai,

353
00:20:05,020 --> 00:20:07,017
your heart had nowhere else to go.

354
00:20:07,100 --> 00:20:09,997
So if you're gonna be mad at
someone, it should be Sanji!

355
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:11,857
You can fix it.

356
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:14,720
Can't you not until your body comes back

357
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:20,517
So they're all here,
mm—hmm, we gotta help.

358
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:21,430
Let's

359
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,897
just forget about them too much work;

360
00:20:28,980 --> 00:20:32,477
all of them are addicted to
drugs, yeah, we know that.

361
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:36,457
I tested them for kids; I want
to take them all back home,

362
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:39,297
but they need to recover
and build up their strength.

363
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:42,637
I don't know if we can do anything
about their size—it's sad.

364
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:46,317
Who would do this to a
bunch of little kids? Well,

365
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:49,797
the world government for one—for
hundreds of years now they've

366
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:53,177
been conducting experiments to
try and turn people into giants.

367
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:58,437
The government, but why would
they do something like that?

368
00:20:58,520 --> 00:21:00,557
If I had to take a guess,

369
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:02,577
then I'd say it's to
create unlimited giant

370
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:05,657
soldiers—it's hard to
beat an army like that.

371
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:11,700
Caesar's probably hoping to figure
out how to do. out how to do

372
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:15,537
at first, so he can beat Vegapunk
and the government to the punch.

373
00:21:15,620 --> 00:21:16,620
But I don't think

374
00:21:20,980 --> 00:21:21,810
it's that simple.

375
00:21:21,893 --> 00:21:23,497
You sure you want to help them?

376
00:21:23,580 --> 00:21:26,497
I mean, you don't even know
who these kids are, do you?

377
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:27,410
We don't.

378
00:21:27,620 --> 00:21:29,957
You're right, they may be strangers to me.

379
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:30,922
But they looked

380
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:34,477
at me with tears in their
eyes, begging for help.

381
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:38,257
The Master was able to trick them
into coming to this terrible place.

382
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:41,340
But once they got here, it
didn't take too long for

383
00:21:45,480 --> 00:21:47,317
them to realize that
something wasn't right.

384
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:50,337
I'm going to make sure
every single one of them is

385
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:53,877
safe and sound, and I won't
leave this island until I do.

386
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:57,254
If I leave with Luffy, are
you going to stay here alone?

387
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:59,106
Wait, I'm not going anywhere.

388
00:21:59,280 --> 00:22:02,440
If this is important to
Nami and Chopper, then I'll

389
00:22:03,180 --> 00:22:04,010
stay too.

390
00:22:04,093 --> 00:22:06,701
And Sanji wants to put
that samurai back together.

391
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:10,377
Look, if you're going to work With
us then, get used to helping people.

392
00:22:10,460 --> 00:22:16,917
You have no idea what you're
getting into here, pal.

393
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:21,137
Here's the thing: see most of the
time when you're forming an alliance,

394
00:22:21,220 --> 00:22:23,057
you have a couple of
groups with a common goal

395
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:24,957
and you negotiate the
best way to get it done.

396
00:22:25,040 --> 00:22:27,057
Does that sound right, obviously?

397
00:22:27,140 --> 00:22:32,637
So you think, but in Luffy's world that
logic gets thrown out the window completely.

398
00:22:32,720 --> 00:22:34,697
Just means I'm friends
with you frankly—you

399
00:22:34,780 --> 00:22:36,637
could forget about having
any say in what we.

400
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:37,550
we do.

401
00:22:37,633 --> 00:22:38,500
It's all up to him.

402
00:22:38,620 --> 00:22:39,560
All up to me.

403
00:22:39,940 --> 00:22:43,017
As soon as this guy makes up his
mind about something, that's it.

404
00:22:43,100 --> 00:22:45,537
You're along for the ride
whether you like it or not.

405
00:22:45,620 --> 00:22:47,208
If selfishness was a power,

406
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:50,857
he'd take out that emperor on the spot.

407
00:22:50,940 --> 00:22:52,680
How do you stand me? Look,

408
00:22:52,880 --> 00:22:55,077
I understand that this is
what your friends want,

409
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:57,640
but that doesn't concern our planet. Hey!

410
00:22:57,980 --> 00:22:59,921
Stop flicking your boogers at me!

411
00:23:01,040 --> 00:23:01,900
That's nasty!

412
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:03,257
Just wipe it off.

413
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:06,740
I can't move right now,
remember? Right, sir.

414
00:23:08,060 --> 00:23:10,140
Fine, but we have to hurry up.

415
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:11,557
There's no time.

416
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:14,517
Putting the samurai back together
can be your group's problem.

417
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:18,377
But I guess I can go investigate the
drug that was given to the children.

418
00:23:18,460 --> 00:23:20,397
Now who's the ship's doctor again?

419
00:23:20,480 --> 00:23:21,480
You come with me.

420
00:23:21,680 --> 00:23:23,974
We'll do research behind Caesar's back.

421
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:30,280
There, that should do it. I'm sorry.

422
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:32,880
It's just, I can't walk right now.

423
00:23:33,080 --> 00:23:34,374
I hope you don't mind.

424
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:40,400
Well, that's a lot of hats, Draghi!

425
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:43,200
Sorry for laughing, but I just...

426
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:45,380
Super cute!

427
00:23:46,860 --> 00:23:48,437
Careful out there, Chopper.

428
00:23:48,520 --> 00:23:49,920
You can count on me.

429
00:23:55,620 --> 00:23:59,149
As you could probably all tell
from those assassins he sent,

430
00:23:59,660 --> 00:24:03,640
Caesar wants to eliminate you, as
well as White Hunter and the G5,

431
00:24:05,180 --> 00:24:06,937
so he can take the children back;

432
00:24:07,020 --> 00:24:12,297
he's not gonna stop pursuing you,
not until he gets what he's after.

433
00:24:12,380 --> 00:24:16,397
Before the incident four years
ago when he became a criminal,

434
00:24:16,480 --> 00:24:18,580
he was a government scientist.

435
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:21,517
Punk hazard is restricted territory;

436
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:23,997
if word gets out that
someone's been living here,

437
00:24:24,080 --> 00:24:26,717
then Caesar will be forced
to leave his perfect hideout;

438
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:29,240
that's why he'll stop at nothing to kill.

439
00:24:29,780 --> 00:24:30,610
all of you.

440
00:24:30,693 --> 00:24:32,849
This is a guy with a
bounty of 300 million.

441
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:35,000
Not only did he eat the Logia-type

442
00:24:35,820 --> 00:24:38,737
Gas-Gas fruit, he's also got
weapons of mass destruction.

443
00:24:38,820 --> 00:24:41,408
Caesar Clown is a force
to be reckoned with.

444
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:45,120
300 million?

445
00:24:45,920 --> 00:24:49,117
Those of you who can't use
Haki should steer clear of him.

446
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:50,540
He's extremely tough.

447
00:24:51,120 --> 00:24:53,200
Well, we do have some Haki users.

448
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:55,520
There's me, Zoro, and Sanji.

449
00:24:55,860 --> 00:24:56,717
Oh, and you.

450
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:58,447
Yeah, that should be enough.

451
00:24:58,640 --> 00:25:00,317
I'll head over to the lab now.

452
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:02,320
Be careful out there. Sure.

453
00:25:02,700 --> 00:25:05,097
So we're supposed to kidnap
this master guy, right?

454
00:25:05,180 --> 00:25:06,817
That's the quickest way to do this?

455
00:25:06,900 --> 00:25:08,018
Yeah, that's right.

456
00:25:08,260 --> 00:25:14,300
Wait, what good will it do us to kidnap
Caesar? Money? Oh, no. That's not it.

457
00:25:14,420 --> 00:25:16,560
Caesar's their boss. That's true.

458
00:25:16,760 --> 00:25:19,257
There wouldn't be anybody
to pay his ransom.

459
00:25:19,340 --> 00:25:22,160
What we're after is chaos, not money. Huh?

460
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:24,230
Chaos?

461
00:25:24,500 --> 00:25:25,797
Sorry, I don't get it.

462
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:27,762
No point in explaining this now.

463
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:31,115
We can worry about what lies
ahead when the time comes.

464
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:35,180
For right now, it's better to
focus on capturing Caesar Clown.

465
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:36,760
It won't be easy.

466
00:25:38,540 --> 00:25:42,599
As soon as that's done, I'll explain
the whole plan to you in detail.

467
00:25:43,480 --> 00:25:44,310
That said,

468
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:50,260
once we get our hands on Caesar, that's
going to set everything in motion.

469
00:25:51,280 --> 00:25:52,400
So be ready.

470
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:54,132
There's no turning back.

471
00:25:57,500 --> 00:25:59,237
Last chance to change your mind.

472
00:25:59,320 --> 00:26:00,517
It's up to you, Straw Hat.

473
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:01,541
Oh, don't worry.

474
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:03,940
I'm still with you. Well, all right.

475
00:26:04,440 --> 00:26:07,322
Then I'm more than willing
to cooperate with you.

476
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:10,798
You just need to make sure
your crew's on board, too.

477
00:26:11,040 --> 00:26:12,500
Uh-huh. Sure thing.

478
00:26:19,380 --> 00:26:20,210
Ah!

479
00:26:20,860 --> 00:26:21,690
Die!

480
00:26:27,160 --> 00:26:30,640
That's Freebar Smoothie,
and Fenbok of the Gourd.

481
00:26:36,100 --> 00:26:37,880
Rope-tugging Chop, too.

482
00:26:38,180 --> 00:26:40,040
I thought so. These people.

483
00:26:40,340 --> 00:26:42,837
As it turns out, they're
all former prisoners.

484
00:26:42,920 --> 00:26:45,391
They just look a little bit different now.

485
00:26:50,820 --> 00:26:52,220
I think you're right.

486
00:26:52,500 --> 00:26:53,917
But what's going on?

487
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:58,176
The report said everyone was killed
during the incident four years ago.

488
00:26:59,700 --> 00:27:00,530
Smokey!

489
00:27:00,613 --> 00:27:02,344
Why do they all look like that?

490
00:27:03,300 --> 00:27:04,200
I don't know.

491
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:06,577
Who gives a damn what they look like?

492
00:27:06,660 --> 00:27:08,895
Just keep holding them back, would ya?

493
00:27:10,460 --> 00:27:12,420
We can't send out a signal!

494
00:27:14,120 --> 00:27:15,800
Until we get to sea!

495
00:27:17,780 --> 00:27:18,610
Fire!

496
00:27:29,880 --> 00:27:31,700
Master, do you have a call?

497
00:27:32,980 --> 00:27:33,810
Sir?

498
00:27:33,893 --> 00:27:35,200
Oh, let it ring.

499
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:38,317
I'm sure it's something
along the lines of we

500
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:41,297
opened the door and something
terrible was inside.

501
00:27:41,380 --> 00:27:43,637
It's killing our comrades left and right.

502
00:27:43,720 --> 00:27:46,640
Oh, Master, please help us, etc., etc.

503
00:27:47,100 --> 00:27:49,159
Why would I want to listen to that?

504
00:27:49,600 --> 00:27:53,541
I never imagined this island would
be graced with so many visitors.

505
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:56,941
There's no need to collect
any more test subjects.

506
00:28:09,780 --> 00:28:11,740
Hello! Master! Master!

507
00:28:13,760 --> 00:28:15,360
Please, pick up quick!

508
00:28:15,880 --> 00:28:17,400
We did what you told us!

509
00:28:17,600 --> 00:28:20,424
We opened up that big
door in the Burning Lands!

510
00:28:22,820 --> 00:28:23,650
No good!

511
00:28:23,920 --> 00:28:25,508
The Master won't answer me!

512
00:28:26,220 --> 00:28:27,050
Oh, no!

513
00:28:27,380 --> 00:28:28,733
It's catching up to us!

514
00:28:28,960 --> 00:28:29,790
What the hell?

515
00:28:29,873 --> 00:28:31,597
How far can that crazy thing run?

516
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:35,033
I don't know, but I don't want
to die like everyone else!

517
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:06,500
We're done for.

518
00:29:06,740 --> 00:29:09,799
That thing's so huge, we're
never going to get away.

519
00:29:34,620 --> 00:29:35,700
No, please!

520
00:29:35,900 --> 00:29:37,260
Please, don't kill me!

521
00:29:37,840 --> 00:29:39,100
Master, why?

522
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:56,000
Oh, yes, that's right.

523
00:29:56,280 --> 00:29:58,045
You don't know my pet, do you?

524
00:29:58,620 --> 00:30:00,280
It's a rare specimen.

525
00:30:00,640 --> 00:30:03,060
Its body is made of deadly slime.

526
00:30:06,940 --> 00:30:07,770
Master!

527
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:14,700
It can be a bit much, but I can't
allow anyone to leave this island.

528
00:30:25,920 --> 00:30:29,300
How does it feel to be
set free after so long?

529
00:30:30,660 --> 00:30:31,490
Smiley!
